Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Order 8", "Section",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.998638517460739*^9, 
  3.998638521561556*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"fc24f842-4bf5-4017-be45-\
fa2fb967a3ea"],

Cell["\<\
The phenomenon of the over-constrained region returns at order n=8 in a \
larger span of cycles q = [15, 26]. Here the true research into the manifolds \
begins, although the analytics are costly. We instead evaluate the Jacobians \
in specific points and compute their properties. We find that the \
\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]accidental\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] solutions \
submanifold gains a degree of freedom at every odd cycle, starting with 0 at \
q=15 like in order n=6. The number of null directions grow, but only in the \
\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]accidental\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] points themselves, \
not everywhere. Once we reach the under-constrained region at q=27, the \
expected behaviour returns and a free parameter is gained at every cycle, \
everywhere on the manifold.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.977487529804587*^9, 3.977487588153356*^9}, {
  3.999596349038378*^9, 3.999596563739216*^9}, {3.9995966013328667`*^9, 
  3.999597081138983*^9}, {3.999597115192089*^9, 
  3.999597363821306*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"357dc8ed-92d8-d44c-ba59-\
5fe47ba94411"],

